<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import MemoPeekProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/memo/MemoPeekProbeDemo.abide"
  import MemoPendingProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/memo/MemoPendingProbeDemo.abide"
  import MemoRefreshingProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/memo/MemoRefreshingProbeDemo.abide"
  import MemoErrorProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/memo/MemoErrorProbeDemo.abide"
  import MemoWatchProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/memo/MemoWatchProbeDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Reactive probes</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every <a href="/memo">memo</a> exposes the same reactive read surface — the <strong>probes</strong>. They are views of one slot's state machine (<em>idle → pending → value | error</em>, with a <code>refreshing</code> flag over a retained value). A <a href="/channel">channel</a> implements the same surface over a lossy hub, so this identical vocabulary shows up on <a href="/rpc/probes">RPC reads</a> (memo + transport) and <a href="/sockets/probes">sockets</a> (channel + transport) too — here each probe runs over a plain client-side <code>memo()</code>, one demo apiece.</p>

  <h2><code>peek()</code> — the non-blocking snapshot</h2>
  <p><code>undefined</code> while the first load is in flight, the value once it resolves. Reading it subscribes the caller and kicks a coalesced load.</p>
  <Demo id="memo-peek" title="<code>memo.peek(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/memo/MemoPeekProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <MemoPeekProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>pending()</code> — the first-load flag</h2>
  <p><strong>yes</strong> only while the first load runs (no value yet); back to <strong>no</strong> once the slot settles.</p>
  <Demo id="memo-pending" title="<code>memo.pending(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/memo/MemoPendingProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <MemoPendingProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>refreshing()</code> — revalidation over a retained value</h2>
  <p>Distinct from <code>pending</code>: <strong>yes</strong> only while a re-fetch runs over a value that stays on screen. Load, then refresh — the value holds, <code>refreshing</code> flips to yes, <code>pending</code> stays no.</p>
  <Demo id="memo-refreshing" title="<code>memo.refreshing(args)</code> vs <code>pending(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/memo/MemoRefreshingProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <MemoRefreshingProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>error()</code> — the retained error</h2>
  <p>A rejected load lands on the slot; <code>error()</code> holds it until an <code>invalidate</code> + successful read clears it.</p>
  <Demo id="memo-error" title="<code>memo.error(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/memo/MemoErrorProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <MemoErrorProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>watch(args, cb)</code> — the method form</h2>
  <p>Runs the callback whenever <em>this slot's</em> value changes (unlike <code>watch(thunk)</code>, which auto-tracks an expression). Every load and refresh fires it.</p>
  <Demo id="memo-watch" title="<code>memo.watch(args, cb)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/memo/MemoWatchProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <MemoWatchProbeDemo />
  </Demo>
</main>
